course: dictionary
lesson: 15150
title: An old word for a classmate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A schoolfellow is a person who goes or went to the same school as you. It is an old-fashioned word, so you will mostly find it in old books, letters and history.
explain: «In her diary, Mary wrote about her schoolfellows.» The word diary and the idea of writing about school are clues. Mary is writing about the children she sat with in class, so schoolfellows must mean people from her school.
explain: Today we use other words for the same idea: classmate, schoolmate or school friend. «Tom met an old schoolfellow at the station.» means Tom met someone he went to school with a long time ago.
fact: A schoolfellow is a person who goes or went to the same school as you.
fact: «Schoolfellow» means the same as «schoolmate».
fact: «Schoolfellow» is old-fashioned; people today usually say «classmate» or «school friend».
fact: Victorian stories often mention schoolfellows.
fact: The phrase «an old schoolfellow» means someone you went to school with long ago.
exercise: «Her schoolfellows came to her wedding.» What does schoolfellows mean? | *People who went to the same school as her | Shopkeepers near the school gate | Teachers who worked at her school | Family members who live near her
exercise: Which modern word means the same as schoolfellow? | Wardrobe | Playground | Headteacher | *Classmate
exercise: «He met an old schoolfellow on the train.» Find and copy the word that means someone who went to the same school. | train | teacher | station | *schoolfellow
test: «Grandma showed us a photo of her schoolfellows from 1950.» What does schoolfellows mean? | Dogs who lived in the yard | *Pupils who shared her school | Ladies who sold sweets in the shop | Neighbours who lived across the road
test: «My old schoolfellow lives across the sea now.» What is an old schoolfellow? | A relative who lives far away | A teacher who has retired | A person who lives in the same street as you | *A person who went to school with you
exam: «Ella and her schoolfellow Sam laughed about the old headmaster.» What is Sam to Ella? | *Someone who went to the same school as her | A dog trainer | A relative of hers | A shopkeeper from the village
